# An and-mask that runs up to the bit below the sign bit keeps x itself
# when x lies in [0, 2^(width−1)). A value whose range reaches below 0 is
# refused, 32- and 64-bit. A parameter's range is unknown and taken as
# nonnegative: n − 256 reads as itself, and is refused once n is bound
# below 256, the store's offset then a uniform variable, a multiple of
# 256. Each kernel's store, past its `.entry` line, prints its address,
# or `addr ?` and why, and its sectors per warp request.
RUN: %ptxroof analyze %fixtures/micro/and_sign_bit.ptx | FileCheck --check-prefix=FREE "%s"
RUN: %ptxroof analyze %fixtures/micro/and_sign_bit.ptx --bind 1:n=100 | FileCheck --check-prefix=BOUND "%s"
FREE: {{^}}.visible .entry micro_and_sign_bit( // block 512×1×1 | pointer params assumed 32 B aligned | per CTA: global store 2,048 B; param load 4,096 B{{$}}
FREE: {{^}}	st.global.u32 	[%rd3], %r1; // global store [64·⌊%tid.x/16⌋ + param_0] sectors/req 2 (ideal 1){{$}}
FREE: {{^}}.visible .entry micro_and_sign_negative( // block 512×1×1 | per CTA: global store 2,048 B; param load 4,096 B{{$}}
FREE: {{^}}	st.global.u32 	[%rd3], %r1; // global store addr ? (and-mask 0x7fffff00 clears bit 31 of a value that may set it){{$}}
FREE: {{^}}.visible .entry micro_and_sign_wide( // block 512×1×1 | per CTA: global store 2,048 B; param load 4,096 B{{$}}
FREE: {{^}}	st.global.u32 	[%rd5], %r1; // global store addr ? (and-mask 0x7fffffffffffff00 clears bit 63 of a value that may set it){{$}}
FREE: {{^}}.visible .entry micro_and_sign_param( // block 512×1×1 | pointer params assumed 32 B aligned | per CTA: global store 2,048 B; param load 6,144 B{{$}}
FREE: {{^}}	st.global.u32 	[%rd3], %r2; // global store [param_0 + 4·param_1 - 4·((param_1 - 256) mod 256) - 1024] sectors/req 1 (ideal 1){{$}}
BOUND: {{^}}.visible .entry micro_and_sign_param( // block 512×1×1 | param_1 = 100 | pointer params assumed 32 B aligned | per CTA: global store 2,048 B; param load 6,144 B{{$}}
BOUND: {{^}}	st.global.u32 	[%rd3], %r2; // global store [4·uniform(%r4@97) + param_0] sectors/req 1 (ideal 1){{$}}
